+## API keys and audit
+
+- `apiKeys` holds `{ key, name, role }`; `role` is `viewer`, `cook` or
+  `manager`. Keys are secrets: they are never returned by the API.
+- `audit` holds one `{ at, keyName, method, path, status }` entry per
+  request that may change data (any method but GET/HEAD/OPTIONS) made with a
+  known key, whatever its outcome. Entries are appended in time order and
+  never edited or deleted.
+- Both are optional in schema 2; a file without them has no keys (every
+  request is refused) and an empty audit log.
+
